On Thursday 29 April 2004 11:26 Bardia (silverknob@hotmail.com) wrote:

> Hey I was wondering, do you need to carry all your spellbooks around
> as a Wizard? I understand if you read a scroll of amneis then you'd
> have to relearn the spells but other than that, is there another
> reason seeing as the books can accumulate and you end up wth no more
> strength to carry anything else.

You can stash them somewhere safe, like in a chest, or a closet, or on
the first level of Sokoban, and come back to them when you need to read
them. Spells time out after ~20.000 turns, so you'll want to relearn
them a few times in a normal game. You get early warning, though.

Some spellbooks are good to have handy in case a spell times out at an
awkward moment; magic missile comes to mind.

